            <ArticleTitle>Usefulness of positron emission tomography in defining myocardial viability in patients referred for cardiac transplantation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1271-4, A9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Positron emission tomography imaging detected evidence of viability in 17 of 33 patients with evidence of infarction only on their thallium scans who were referred for transplant evaluation. Eleven of these 17 underwent revascularization with excellent outcome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
